@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# VetConnect integrated source candidate | 26 November 2026
+Release status: HOLD. This is an actual source archive with limited additional changes, not a fully tested production build or database dump.
+
+## Comparison and decisions
+The uploaded source has PR162 company directory code and existing admin overview, permission gates, master data studio, public profiles, migrations and CI. The closure ZIP contains requirements, historical SQL references and 80 acceptance cases. Preserve existing migrations byte-for-byte. Historical dry-run SQL is not a new migration and is deliberately not imported. No live changes. Compare this candidate with fresh GitHub main before merging; do not overwrite newer commits.
+
+## Implemented locally
+- Shared compact company description and case-insensitive exact label deduplication; use on directory and profile; no full description in hero; parent category options for exact existing child labels. Existing underlying descriptions are preserved.
+- Newest pending records on admin overview/approvals using existing permission-gated activity sources and review links. Shows up to 12 recent pending entries; not a complete queue or real-time push. Remove visible raw UUID prefix from flagged account labels.
+- Four executable pure logic regression tests. Existing 80-case manual acceptance matrix and read-only SQL audit included.
+
+## Engineering workstreams still open
+| Discipline | Required change | Gate |
+|---|---|---|
+| Database architect | Reuse companies.id, master_data_items parent hierarchy, geo_areas and aliases. Reconcile legacy company user links; no guessed taxonomy. Stable sector/subsector/activity, disease, vaccine, species, brand, breed, quality/certification, market and geography dimensions; explicit many-to-many links. | Isolated migration, backfill report, unique constraints, rollback, RLS two-account tests |
+| Backend | Shared transactional create/edit/publish/unpublish/archive/restore; dependency-checked delete with confirmation, audit and permissions. Scoped secure drafts, idempotency, bounded paginated API, safe export. | Save/reload, failed submit, authorization and concurrency tests |
+| Search | One public search across approved vets, companies, feeds, medicines, vaccines, labs, jobs and professionals; aliases and exact disease distinction. Example Poultry > vaccine > disease > product > company; feed > nutrition > supplier; HR > job > employer and verified professional. Use relationships, not keyword guesses. | Exact matches, related separately labelled, privacy and performance |
+| Admin | Unified queues with new/pending/approved/rejected/published/archived, independent PVMC and publication checks; new submissions alerts, owner/assignee, review date, click-through dossier, safe edit/archive/restore/delete, bulk operations only with explicit permission. | Every role, type and lifecycle tested; no false counts |
+| Senior UX/graphic design | Preserve navy/orange identity and original uploaded logos/photos. Shared spacing (4/8/12/16/24/32), card alignment, type hierarchy, visible focus, accessible contrast, consistent 1/2/3-column grids, concise titles, contextual empty/error states, no redundant labels or internal IDs. Audit every route listed in ROUTES.txt at 360/390/768/1366px. | Screenshot evidence and keyboard navigation, no overflow |
+| Reporting and social | Permission-scoped CSV/print/PDF, public links and editable captions/hashtags; social share composer with user confirmation, no automatic posts or private data transmission. Browser print already exists; full exports and posting integrations not verified. | Export injection prevention, private field allowlists, destination confirmation |
+| Security | RLS policy review, API field allowlists, private evidence, dependency audit, no secrets in ZIP, exact-head test gates. Hide raw identifiers visually but retain relational keys and audit metadata. | Anonymous/owner/unrelated/admin test matrix; no production test data |
+| Performance | Measure current and candidate mobile/desktop; database indexed server filters and pagination, bounded admin query fan-out, image optimization, optional map links; preserve AdSense and approved assets. Targets proposed: LCP <=2.5s, INP <=200ms, CLS <=0.1 at p75; measure rather than claim. | Record measurements and regressions |
+| Release | No new feature scope until P0/P1 gates pass. Verify exact GitHub main and both Vercel custom aliases; inspect automatic domain assignment, preserve rollback, staged schema compatibility. | Successful exact-head CI, staged DB, manual acceptance, both aliases verified |
+
+## Testing status
+Archive integrity: both inputs passed. Structure audit: 96 required entries verified. New helper tests: 4/4 passed. Source release gate passed before adding this report; rerun after all changes. npm ci --offline failed ENOTCACHED for zod-validation-error 4.0.2; full lint/typecheck/build/database tests not verified. No browser screenshots or actual latency measurements. No production database modifications, no live posting or deployment. All existing migrations are historical source, not a current production schema export.
+
+## How to integrate
+Extract outside your checkout. Compare exact current main with this source (especially the five changed source/test files and added docs). Apply only reviewed changes on a branch, not a blind ZIP overwrite. Install dependencies in a network-enabled trusted CI environment using npm ci; run npm run check, npm run security:audit, and node --experimental-strip-types --test scripts/directory-presentation.test.mjs. Rehearse existing and proposed migrations on isolated staging; complete acceptance.csv and store results. Never upload ZIP as a repository artifact or run historical SQL on production. Promote one verified build only after all gates and review.
